  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>The IRGC Navy declared a formal closure of the Strait of Hormuz on July 12 "until further notice, pending cessation of US military interventions." Windward AI registered zero commercial vessel transits over 10,000 DWT with AIS transponders active since July 7. US CENTCOM reinstated a naval blockade effective Tuesday, July 14, adding a second constraint to commercial shipping access. IMF PortWatch had recorded approximately 34 transits per day as of July 5 — 60 percent below the pre-war average of 88/day and well short of the 20/day 7-day rolling average required for resolution. → moved <span class="cite">F11</span></p>
      <p>On July 12, Iranian-attributed strikes hit targets in Bahrain, Kuwait, Jordan, Qatar, and Oman. On July 13, IRGC naval forces struck two UAE-flagged supertankers in Omani territorial waters; UAE maritime authorities confirmed one crew fatality. The IRGC issued a formal Hormuz closure announcement that same evening, citing ongoing US strikes on Iranian territory as justification. These events establish a documented record of Iranian state force applied against GCC-member assets within the seven-day window before F13's horizon date, and the HUMAN_REVIEW_FLAG on F13 requires a human determination on whether resolution criteria were already met on July 13. → moved <span class="cite">F13</span></p>
      <p>Trump stated on July 10 that Washington had agreed to Iran's request to continue negotiations, while maintaining that the June 17 ceasefire was concluded. Pakistan and Qatar remain active as mediators, with logistics infrastructure from the Bürgenstock process intact. The Islamabad MoU 60-day negotiating window runs to approximately August 16 (June 17 plus 60 days). Crude oil closed at $118 per barrel on July 13 — a nine-percent gain attributed to the Hormuz closure and conflict risk premium — creating economic pressure on both sides. → supports <span class="cite">F10</span> without move</p>
      <p>The sixth round of US-brokered Israel-Lebanon talks opened in Rome on July 14. Lebanon's delegation conditioned full participation on Israeli withdrawal from two pilot zones; Israel's delegation attended without new concessions on the withdrawal timeline. Hezbollah Secretary-General Naim Qassem described the entire framework as "null and void" in a statement carried by Al-Manar on July 13. Lebanon's President Aoun is scheduled to visit Washington on July 21. → supports <span class="cite">F9</span> without move</p>
      <p>The Knesset is scheduled to formally dissolve on July 17, with elections confirmed for the mandatory date of October 27. The dissolution law reached its first reading with a 106-0 vote on June 2; final reading passage is expected this week with Ben-Gvir and Smotrich remaining in coalition. Haaretz and Times of Israel confirmed on July 12 that no election date earlier than October 27 had been proposed or accepted by the ruling coalition. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

