      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (40%):</strong> Pakistan and Qatar mediators remain engaged and the Islamabad MoU window runs to August 16 — sufficient to contain hostilities below the threshold of GCC ground operations while preventing a full diplomatic breakthrough.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> A new ceasefire or MoU revival (F10, 45%) that includes a Hormuz reopening framework is the most plausible near-term deescalation trigger, but the 31-day window is tight against active US bombing operations.</p>
