  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>State media characterizations of the July 12–13 GCC operations diverged from Western TIER1 framing. IRNA and Tasnim ran the Bahrain and Kuwait strikes under the category "defensive deterrence operations," while Fars headlined the Bahrain incident as "legitimate resistance to American siege." Press TV's English-language service ran commentary labeling the maritime operation a "graduated defensive escalation," though this formulation does not appear verbatim in Farsi IRNA text — a standard divergence between export-facing and domestic-audience output. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>IRIB's primetime broadcast on July 13 gave extended coverage to the Hormuz closure announcement. Araghchi's statement to parliament described the restriction as "temporary, pending US military withdrawal," while IRNA's Farsi coverage did not include the "temporary" qualifier. Khamenei-adjacent commentary on Tasnim's opinion pages framed the closure as a "corrective measure" whose duration lay in Washington's hands — a formulation that does not appear in the official IRNA wire. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Kayhan's July 14 editorial, headlined "The American-Zionist Project Has Hit a Wall," argued that IRGC GCC strikes had drawn attention to the limitations of the Abraham Accords security architecture without adding a forward-looking assessment. Iranian state media ran no coverage of the Rome Israel-Lebanon talks in its July 14 broadcasts; Tasnim carried a brief noting Qassem's rejection of the Lebanon framework and placed it under "Iranian-Lebanese resistance solidarity." → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

